.TH WERKMEISTER-MACHINE-MIGRATE 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-machine\-migrate \- Move ~/.sandbox to ~/.werkmeister and repoint everything that names it: config.yaml, env.sh, the ~/.zshenv block, services.yaml, the pr\-watch schedule and workspace compose files; then rewrite workspace hooks, permission rules and with\-temp\-home, secrets.env and Claude Desktop's args to the noun\-group spellings. Safe to re\-run; refuses while affected containers are running. \" name-check: ignore
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister machine migrate\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-workspaces\fR
Also rename each workspace's .sandbox/ to .werkmeister/. \" name-check: ignore
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Report what would change without writing.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A one\-shot move of the pre\-rename machine folder to \fB~/.werkmeister\fR, repointing every file that carries the old path. Safe to re\-run; it refuses while containers the move would break are running. Pull and rebuild the CLI before you migrate.
.PP
It also brings what an older CLI wrote up to the noun\-group spellings (SW\-186): each workspace's hooks, permission rules and \fBwith\-temp\-home\fR, the stale \fBSANDBOX_MCP_TOKEN\fR in \fBsecrets.env\fR, and Claude Desktop's server args. A workspace whose \fB.env\fR still exports only \fBSANDBOX_FEATURE\fR is listed; run \fBwerkmeister workspace init\fR there. \" name-check: ignore
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister machine migrate \-\-check
werkmeister machine migrate \-\-workspaces
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
